Title:  Version 19.4.0

Seq:    13.1

Level:  3 - chapter

Class:  version

Date:   2026-07-28

Teaser:

Alternating row colors on the List tab are now optional; A Nav menu item to go Home (top of list) has been added; An author title may now be included in a Quote-From citation; Added an Image-Class field that can be used to apply a class to an image identified in the Image Name field; Single quotes around values are now removed when reading a Note from disk, to increase compatibility with YAML processing conventions.

Timestamp: 20260716190601

Body:

##### Alternating Row Colors Now Optional

The [[App Settings]] now contain an option, as part of the [[Other Settings]], to turn off the alternating row colors on the List tab. 

##### Home Navigation Command Added

The *Nav* menu now contains a *Home* function that will return the user to the first note in the current Collection, duplicating the function of the Home button in the Toolbar. The command has a keyboard shortcut of Shift-Cmd-H. 

##### Author Title added as Optional Parm for Quote Citation

When using the Markdown command to [[Format a Quote Citation]], the Title of the author/speaker may now be specified as the first parameter following the name of the Author.

##### Added an Image Class Field

[[Image Class]] can be used as a field label in order to specify a CSS class value to be assigned to an `img` tag.

##### Stripping of Single Quotes Around Values

Since other processors sometimes emit values enclosed in single quotes, Notenik now looks for these and strips them when found. 

